{
  "_id": "tg-swearing",
  "content": [
    {
      "text": "Beer-sheba; because there they sware, Gen. 21:31. I did swear to give it to Abraham, Ex. 6:8. which he sware unto thy fathers to give thee, a land, Ex. 13:5. not take the name of the Lord thy God in vain, Ex. 20:7. not swear by my name falsely, Lev. 19:12. Lord … sware that I should not go over Jordan, Deut. 4:21. Thou … shalt swear by his name, Deut. 6:13. possess the good land which the Lord sware unto thy fathers, Deut. 6:18. hath not lifted up his soul unto vanity, nor sworn deceitfully, Ps. 24:4. I sware in my wrath, Ps. 95:11 (Heb. 3:11; 4:3). Lord hath sworn, and will not repent, Ps. 110:4 (Heb. 7:21). Lord hath sworn in truth, Ps. 132:11 (Acts 2:30). every knee shall bow, every tongue shall swear, Isa. 45:23. swear … but not in truth, Isa. 48:1 (1 Ne. 20:1). how should my name be polluted, Isa. 48:11. Lord hath sworn by his right hand, Isa. 62:8. he that sweareth in the earth shall swear by the God of truth, Isa. 65:16. surely they swear falsely, Jer. 5:2. because of swearing the land mourneth, Jer. 23:10. sware by him that liveth for ever, Dan. 12:7 (Rev. 10:6). By swearing … they break out, Hosea 4:2. They have spoken words, swearing falsely, Hosea 10:4. Lord God hath sworn by his holiness, Amos 4:2. They that swear by the sin of Samaria, Amos 8:14. every one that sweareth shall be cut off, Zech. 5:3. swift witness … against false swearers, Mal. 3:5 (3 Ne. 24:5).",
